narrative:
## Programming a Robot With Commands

A robot processes a sequence of commands. Each command carries its own data (distance, degrees, message, seconds) and produces a string output when executed.

### The Command Enum

```xiom
enum Command {
  Move(distance: Int),
  Turn(degrees: Int),
  Speak(msg: Str),
  Wait(seconds: Int),
}
```

### Creating Commands

```xiom
let cmd1 = Command.Move(10);
let cmd2 = Command.Turn(90);
let cmd3 = Command.Speak("Hello!");
let cmd4 = Command.Wait(2);
```

### Executing a Single Command

Match on the command variant and return a description of what happened:

```xiom
fn execute(cmd: Command) -> Str {
  match cmd {
    Move(dist) => { return "Moving forward " + dist + " steps"; }
    Turn(deg) => { return "Turning " + deg + " degrees"; }
    Speak(msg) => { return "Robot says: " + msg; }
    Wait(sec) => { return "Waiting " + sec + " seconds"; }
  }
}
```

### Running a Command Sequence

Process four commands in order:

```xiom
var log = "";
log = execute(Command.Move(5));
log = execute(Command.Turn(180));
log = execute(Command.Speak("I am here!"));
log = execute(Command.Wait(1));
```

### Tracking Robot State

```xiom
type Robot = {
  x: Int;
  y: Int;
}

fn Robot.process(self, cmd: Command) -> Str {
  match cmd {
    Move(dist) => {
      x = x + dist;
      return "Moved to (" + x + ", " + y + ")";
    }
    _ => { return execute(cmd); }
  }
}
```

